t is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: <span class=\"bullet\">Listen to the audio.</span> <span class=\"bullet\">Type in the missing comparatives and superlatives based on the information you heard. </span><span class=\"bullet\">Use capital letters where necessary.</span>  "}]}]}, {"stimuli_ids": [], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0, "selected": 0}, {"correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 1, "selected": 0}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}]}]}], "type": "RSLT", "id": 11, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": []}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}]}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn6le13ob03re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn6le13ob03re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn6le13ob03re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn6le13ob03re2img01.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "Think about a party you attended. Who spoke more, the men or the women? Who talked the most? Who talked the least? Have you been to a party where only the women contributed to the conversation? Maybe you haven't experienced this situation. Many people think that women are more talkative than men. Is this true? The research suggests that women are not always more outgoing."}, {"time": "22800", "image": "engenn6le13ob03re2img01.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "Some studies have found that women are more talkative than men, but most studies have suggested that men actually talk more than women. How can these differences be explained?"}, {"time": "32200", "image": "engenn6le13ob03re2img01.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "The social setting determines which sex will talk more. In the workplace, men talk more when they are in a high position of authority."}, {"time": "39800", "image": "engenn6le13ob03re2img01.jpg", "id": 4, "text": "In the classroom, female students spoke less, although this depended on the gender of the teacher. Males were more likely to participate in class discussions if the teacher was a woman, but males and females talked the same amount if the teacher was a man."}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Gender Issues"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Who Talks More?"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 13}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe  routines and regular activities in a wider range of social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le13ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "suitable"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "good for, appropriate for"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Men's and women's brains have developed in ways suitable to the jobs their ancestors did hundreds of thousands of years ago. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le13ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about research on men and women."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "talkative"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "describes a person who enjoys talking"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Some studies have found that women are more talkative than men."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le13ob03aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "suggest"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to argue; to try to prove (in research)"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Most studies have suggested that men actually talk more than women. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le13ob03aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "authority"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "responsibility for the work of other people"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Men talk more when they are in a high position of authority."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le13ob03aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "gender"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "sex (male or female)"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Male students spoke more, although this depended on the gender of the teacher. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le13ob03aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "social setting"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " the context you are in, with other people"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The social setting determines which sex will talk more. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le13ob03aud06"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Perfect vs. Simple Past Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about actions you have done at some point in your life that may happen in the future"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the Simple Past tense to talk about a finished action or event. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use the Present Perfect there is a connection between what happened in the past and now. You use time markers like for, since and ever with the Present Perfect."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use the past simple, the time is always past. You use time markers with the past like: then, ago, yesterday, when I was\u2026 with the Simple Past."}, {"type": "text", "content": "To form the Present Perfect tense, you use have/has + the past participle of the base form of the verb."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Comparatives and Superlatives"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are different ways to compare by using adjectives. Two of these are comparatives and superlatives."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Some adjectives change to different words in the comparative and  superlative form. <br> <br>With one syllable words, you add <span class=\"strong\">-er </span>to the adjective to make the comparative form. You add <span class=\"strong\">-est</span> to the adjective to make the superlative form.  <br><br>With words of two or more syllables, you add the word <span class=\"italic\">more</span> before the adjective or adverb in the comparative form. You add <span class=\"italic\">the most</span> before the adjective or the adverb in the superlative form."}, {"type": "text", "content": " <span class =\"strong\">Comparatives</span>: When you compare two things, you use comparatives. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For short adjectives, we add <span class=\"italic\">~er (quieter, smarter, bigger)</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For long adjectives, we use the expression <span class =\"strong\">more + adjective</span> (more intelligent, more interesting, more difficult). "}, {"type": "text", "content": "If we mention the two items for comparison, we use the expression than."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class =\"strong\">Examples</span>:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">At work, women are <span class =\"strong\">quieter than</span> men. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">Women are <span class =\"strong\">more talkative than</span> men at home.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " <span class =\"strong\">Superlatives</span>: You can also use adjectives to compare one item with the rest of a group."}, {"type": "text", "content": "These are called superlative adjectives. For short adjectives, we use the article the and add <span class=\"italic\">~est (the quietest, the smartest, the biggest)</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For long adjectives, we use the expression <span class =\"strong\">the most + adjective</span> <span class=\"italic\">(the most intelligent, the most interesting, the most difficult)</span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class =\"strong\">Examples</span>:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "She was the smartest student in the group; John was the most modest. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "David was the most talkative member of the group."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write down the conclusions of the research on men and women you read in this lesson."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Explain the conclusions to a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "With your partner, discuss possible explanations for these results."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For each research conclusion, write down the best explanation you came up with. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Go online to see if you are correct, or to find the true reason."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write the conclusions of research."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I explain the research conclusions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I discuss possible explanations."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I find the true explanations."}]}]}